Tip: Add indexes on frequently filtered columns:

CREATE INDEX idx_north_customer ON sales_north(customer_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_south_customer ON sales_south(customer_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_west_customer  ON sales_west(cust_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_vw_date_region ON sales_north(sale_date), sales_south(sale_date), sales_west(sold_on);


(MySQL doesn’t index a view directly; index underlying tables.)



🧠 Summary
Aliases normalize schema and make queries readable.
UNION vs UNION ALL: dedupe vs keep all (and speed).
INTERSECT / MINUS in MySQL → use JOIN patterns:
INTERSECT → INNER JOIN on key columns
MINUS/EXCEPT → LEFT JOIN ... IS NULL
Build views to centralize normalization; aggregate and filter on top.
